"Refined design (2026-08-09, answering layering objection): the entity! macro NEVER resolves names or any app concept. It generates a selector enum per invocation, generic over an app-declared external-ref type E (new macro input, e.g. 'type ExternalRef = ...'): EntityIdSelector { Literal(EntityId), Local(u32), External(E) }. E must be SpacetimeType (stored in blob tables). Resolution is dependency-injected: macro generates a resolver trait with resolve_external(&E) -> Result<EntityId, String> (+ batch-local id list handled by instantiation machinery for Local); the APP implements it -- interim impl may use from_name, switching to named-asset-table lookup when replace-namecomponent-with-per-kind-named-asset-tables lands. Literal never consults the resolver. Blob-consuming fns (instantiate_blob, insert_/update_/upsert_ taking blobs) gain a resolver param and return Result (standard propagation, no panics). The _new convenience fns keep raw declared field types (real EntityIds from live handles) and construct components directly with the handle id -- no selector, infallible, unchanged signatures. From<Component> for Blob produces Literal(own referenced id). Naming: avoid 'ctx' (stdb ReducerContext convention); proposed param name 'resolver' (trait e.g. ResolveEntityRef), pending user confirmation."